    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20711?c=uic": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty (Open Rank) /Clinical Pharmacist, Coordinator, Hospital Pharmacy Services",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty (Open Rank) /Clinical Pharmacist, Coordinator, Hospital Pharmacy Services | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Clinical Faculty (Open Rank) /Clinical Pharmacist, Coordinator, Hospital Pharmacy Services Chicago, IL, United States | 1042630 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/2/2026 - Application Deadline: 10/16/2026 Back to Search Clinical Faculty\n(Open Rank) /Clinical Pharmacist, Coordinator, Hospital Pharmacy Services Hiring Department : Pharmacy Practice Location :  Chicago Requisition ID : 1042630 Posting Close Date : Friday, October 16, 2026 Salary: The\nbudgeted salary rate for the position is $135,000 - $160,000. Salary is\ncompetitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also\nconsidering internal equity. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Summary/Description: The\nUIC Retzky College of Pharmacy, Department of Pharmacy Practice is seeking a\nfull-time, motivated professional for the position of Clinical Faculty (Open\nRank)/Clinical Pharmacist, Coordinator, Hospital Pharmacy Services who will be\nassigned to UI Health’s Central Pharmacy. The\nideal candidate will work within the Hospital Pharmacy Operations and team and\nwill be responsible for providing pharmaceutical care to patients at the\nUniversity of Illinois Hospital. The hospital is a 450-bed academic institution\nlocated approximately 2 miles west of downtown Chicago. The hospital serves an\nurban, indigent patient population. The Retzky College of Pharmacy, with campuses in Chicago and Rockford, is the\n#1 college of pharmacy in Illinois and #6 in total research grant funding,\naccording to the American Association of Colleges of Pharmacy (AACP). More\ninformation about the College and Department of Pharmacy Practice can be found\nat https://pharmacy.uic.edu and https://dpp.pharmacy.uic.edu. Duties: Oversee\n     compliance with USP <797>, USP <800>, state and federal\n     regulations, accreditation standards, and organizational policies. Provide\n     leadership and day-to-day support to pharmacists and pharmacy technicians\n     working in sterile compounding areas. Monitor and\n     maintain cleanroom environmental controls, including temperature,\n     humidity, pressure differentials, certification schedules, and\n     environmental monitoring programs. Develop, review,\n     and maintain cleanroom policies, procedures, workflows, and documentation. Lead quality\n     assurance and quality improvement initiatives related to sterile\n     compounding, cleanroom practices, and medication safety. Investigate\n     cleanroom deviations, contamination events, sterility concerns, and\n     medication-related incidents; implement corrective and preventive actions\n     as needed. Ensure proper\n     inventory management of cleanroom supplies, hazardous drug products,\n     sterile compounding materials, and equipment. Conduct routine\n     audits of compounding records, cleaning logs, environmental monitoring\n     results, and staff documentation to ensure compliance. Analyze\n     operational metrics and identify opportunities to improve efficiency,\n     quality, regulatory compliance, and customer service. Assist with\n     implementation of new technologies, workflows, medications, and services\n     related to sterile and hazardous drug compounding. Participate in\n     regulatory inspections, accreditation surveys, and internal audits,\n     including preparation of required documentation and corrective action\n     plans. Serve as a\n     subject matter expert and resource for sterile compounding, cleanroom\n     operations, hazardous drug handling, and pharmacy regulatory requirements. Coordinator\nresponsibilities include, but are not limited to: Coordinate daily\n     sterile compounding and cleanroom operations to ensure safe, efficient,\n     and compliant medication preparation. Coordinate\n     content development and training activities for pharmacy specific\n     educational and clinical programs targeted for students, residents,\n     fellows, and faculty; areas of focus include clinical skill development,\n     provision of clinical pharmacy services, experiential education and\n     critical thinking/problem solving. Responsible for\n     all pharmacy operational, educational, clinical, and business aspects for\n     areas of responsibility; these include addressing and coordinating patient\n     management issues; fiscal operations; scheduling; staff recruiting,\n     orientation, training and development; monitoring workflow; and ensuring\n     appropriate pharmacist and technical staffing in patient care areas. Ensure\n     compliance with pharmacy specific standards such as Accreditation Council\n     for Pharmacy Education (ACPE), Health Insurance Portability and\n     Accountability Act 1996 (HIPAA), The Joint Commission (TJC) and\n     Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA). Institute/coordinate\n     quality control mechanisms to ensure the availability and appropriate use\n     of pharmaceuticals, including investigational drugs; utilize continuous\n     quality improvement in this process; oversee medication management in the\n     Hospital Pharmacy Services. Evaluate and\n     implement new departmental pharmacy information systems to maximize\n     efficiency and achieve the goals of the unit. Coordinate\n     equipment maintenance, calibration, certification, and repair activities\n     for cleanroom and compounding devices. Coordinate\n     personnel training, competency assessments, and ongoing education for\n     pharmacists and pharmacy technicians involved in sterile compounding. Minimum Qualifications: PharmD degree\n     from an ACPE accredited Doctor of Pharmacy Program. Completion of\n     Post Graduate Year 1 (PGY1) pharmacy residency required. Minimum of 3 years’ experience in\n     a hospital pharmacy setting and/or leadership role in lieu of completion\n     of a post graduate year 1 residency and/or fellowship Must present\n     evidence of, or eligibility for, Illinois licensure as a professional\n     pharmacist by start date. Must possess\n     knowledge and skills such that they qualify for a non-tenured clinical\n     faculty position within the Department of Pharmacy Practice at the UIC\n     College of Pharmacy. Academic rank commensurate with experience. Ability\n     to foster a\n     collaborative environment and effectively partner with others towards a\n     common goal Preferred\nQualifications: Advanced knowledge of USP <797>, USP <800>, sterile compounding practices, and cleanroom operations. Strong clinical knowledge base; analytical and problem-solving skills; strong verbal and written communication skills; ability to consistently meet deadlines; demonstrate flexibility and ability to work independently and adapt to a changing work environment; excellent planning, time management and organizational skills. Board\n     certification For fullest consideration, submit a completed application by Friday,\nOctober 16, 2026. A letter of intent and current curriculum vitae must be attached to the\napplication. The names and e-mail contact information of three professional\nreferences must be submitted directly into the application. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
