    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20975?c=uic": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Physics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Physics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant Professor - Physics Chicago, IL, United States | 1042940 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/24/2026 - Application Deadline: 11/16/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor - Physics Hiring Department : Physics Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1042940 Posting Close Date : November 16, 2026 Salary: The budgeted salary range for the position is $100,000 to $120,000. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary The Department of Physics and the\nCollege of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS) at the University of Illinois Chicago invite applications for a tenure-track position in theoretical condensed matter\nphysics at the Assistant Professor level.\nThe emphasis of this search is to strengthen the Department’s efforts in theoretical\ncondensed matter research in quantum materials. The anticipated start date is\nFall 2027. The open faculty position is in the field of computational\nquantum materials, with an emphasis on incorporating artificial intelligence\n(AI) and machine learning (ML) methods. We seek a researcher who will develop\nnew computational approaches that combine physics-based modeling, large-scale\nsimulation, and AI/ML to discover and design materials with quantum properties.\nThe overall objective is to develop predictive and experimentally testable\napproaches to the discovery, understanding, and engineering of quantum\nmaterials, including materials and structures relevant to qubits, quantum\nsensing, and other quantum technologies, with an emphasis on applications in quantum\ninformation science (QIS). The successful candidate is expected to establish a highly\nvisible and externally funded research program addressing questions at the\nintersection of quantum materials, computational physics, and artificial\nintelligence. Research directions may include: -Physics-informed, AI/ML-guided discovery and design of materials exhibiting desirable quantum properties. -Advanced computational approaches to model realistic quantum materials, such as correlated or topological systems, engineered quantum systems and heterostructures, as well as low-dimensional systems relevant to QIS. The\nsuccessful candidate should be able to collaborate with existing condensed\nmatter theoretical and experimental groups in the Department of Physics. The\nmaterials and condensed matter faculty conduct research on a wide range of\nfunctional and complex materials, including energy-relevant, quantum,\ntopological, superconducting, and strongly correlated systems. A fuller\ndescription of the research programs in the Department of Physics can be found\nat phys.uic.edu. UIC offers a strong infrastructure for computational and experimental materials research, including advanced characterization core facilities and substantial high-performance computing capabilities that support large-scale simulations and data-intensive research. The Chicago region has become a national leader in QIS research, supported by robust academic, state, federal, and industrial investments. Existing programs include the Superconducting Quantum Materials and Systems (SQMS) Center, the FermiForward partnership, and the Chicago Quantum Exchange (CQE). UIC is well positioned to play a leading role in this ecosystem. Duties & Responsibilities The assistant professor is\nexpected to establish a highly visible and externally funded research program\nat the forefront of theoretical condensed matter physics. This program should\ninclude the education and participation of doctoral graduate students in\ncutting-edge research projects as well as provide appropriate research\nopportunities for undergraduate students.  The candidate is expected to demonstrate a commitment to teaching\nphysics at both undergraduate and graduate levels within a Research 1\nuniversity environment with a focus on establishing an inclusive and diverse\nenvironment for historically underserved students.  The candidate is also expected to advise\nstudents, and provide service to the department, college and university. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Physics or a related\nfield; or international equivalent Preferred Qualifications Post-Ph.D.\nexperience Required documents to be uploaded include a CV, publication list, and concise statements of research and teaching interests. Applicants who are confirmed to meet the minimum qualifications will be requested to provide contact information for at least three reference letters. Applications must be completed by November 16, 2026, to receive full consideration. Final authorization of the position is subject to the availability of funding. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
