    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20927?c=uic": {
      "title": "Maternal Fetal Medicine Specialist - Open Rank Faculty",
      "description": "Maternal Fetal Medicine Specialist - Open Rank Faculty | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Maternal Fetal Medicine Specialist - Open Rank Faculty Chicago, IL, United States | 1042739 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/22/2026 - Application Deadline: 10/31/2026 Back to Search Maternal Fetal Medicine Specialist - Open Rank Faculty Hiring Department : Obstetrics and Gynecology Location : Chicago, IL Requisition ID :1042739 Posting Close Date: October 31, 2026 Salary: The budgeted salary range for the position is $340,000 to $360,000. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also considering internal equity. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Illinois Chicago is seeking a board-certified/board-eligible Maternal-Fetal Medicine physician to join the Division of Maternal-Fetal Medicine. Academic rank and compensation will be commensurate with experience. The successful candidate will provide comprehensive clinical care for high-risk obstetric patients, engage in teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, and fellows, and contribute to ongoing research and scholarly activity within the department. The Division of MFM supports an ABOG-accredited MFM fellowship and serves as an Administrative Perinatal Network hospital for the State of Illinois. Candidates with clinical or academic interests in ultrasound, perinatal psychiatry, or human genetics and genomics are encouraged to apply. Duties & Responsibilities Provide on- and off-site MFM clinical coverage as attending physician in inpatient and outpatient settings. Provide on- and off-site obstetrical sonography clinical coverage, including interpretation and performance of ultrasound studies, as appropriate. Perform ambulatory and procedural services, including amniocentesis, chorionic villus sampling (CVS), fetal echocardiography, and cerclage placement. Supervise Maternal-Fetal Medicine fellows during Labor and Delivery rotations and other assigned clinical activities. Provide antepartum inpatient service coverage as the attending physician. Participate in out-of-house call coverage for MFM consultations and maternal transports, as assigned. Develop and deliver didactic education for medical students, residents, and MFM fellows. Mentor medical students, residents, MFM fellows, and faculty in clinical care, education, research, and scholarly activities. Participate in maternal morbidity and mortality conferences, including activities at affiliated and network hospitals. This position does not require in-house night call. Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications MD or equivalent Board-certification in Obstetrics and Gynecology from the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology (ABOG) Board-certification or eligibility in Maternal-Fetal Medicine from the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology (ABOG) Eligible for unrestricted medical licensure in the State of Illinois Review of candidates will begin immediately. For fullest consideration, submit CV, cover letter, and names of three referencesdirectly on our site. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20555?c=uic": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant/Associate/Professor - Managerial Studies",
      "description": "Teaching Assistant/Associate/Professor - Managerial Studies | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Teaching Assistant/Associate/Professor - Managerial Studies Chicago, IL, United States | 1042264 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/22/2026 - Application Deadline: 10/26/2026 Back to Search Teaching Assistant/Associate/Professor - Managerial Studies Hiring Department : Managerial Studies Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1042264 Posting Close Date : October 26, 2026 Salary: The budgeted salary range for this position is $100,000 - $125,000\nannually. Salary is commensurate with experience and rank. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. About\nthe University of Illinois Chicago: Located\nin the heart of Chicago, UIC is the city’s largest university and a Tier 1\nresearch institution. UIC is recognized as one of the nation’s most ethnically,\nculturally, and economically diverse campuses and is designated as a Minority\nServing Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific\nIslander Serving Institution (AANAPSI), and a Hispanic Serving Institution\n(HSI). In the 2026 rankings of colleges and universities released by U.S. News\n& World Report, UIC was ranked 42nd overall among public schools\nin the U.S. and first in Illinois for social mobility. UIC was also ranked as\nthe top university in Illinois for value and social mobility in the Wall Street\nJournal/College Pulse 2025 Best Colleges in the U.S. ranking. UIC thus prides\nitself on its mission “to provide the broadest access to the highest levels\nof educational, research, and clinical excellence.” Position\nSummary The\nUniversity of Illinois Chicago College of Business Administration invites\napplications for an open-rank, non-tenure-track position as Teaching Assistant\nProfessor, Teaching  Associate Professor,\nor Teaching Professor in the Managerial Studies Department. UIC's Managerial\nStudies Department offers undergraduate degrees in Management, Human Resource\nManagement, and Entrepreneurship, and teaches the integrated capstone course\nfor undergraduate students in the College of Business. The department also\ncovers various courses in the MBA programs, including courses in the new online\nMBA, as well as courses in the soon-to-be-launched online MSHRM program. The\ndepartment seeks candidates passionate about teaching and promoting student\nsuccess at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Duties\nand Responsibilities: Teaching courses to undergraduate and/or graduate students Teaching responsibilities for the current openings include various courses within the areas of Business and Organization Management, Organizational Behavior and Human Resource Management, Strategic Management, etc. Candidates with experience or interest in teaching topics in these and related areas are encouraged to apply. In addition, candidates who have experience with new and emerging data analysis tools and related decision-making in any teaching area should indicate this in their application. Providing service to the department, college, and university Contributing to the broader mission of the College through industry outreach, student engagement and activities, and professional development/scholarly activities Performing other professional and/or academic activities and special projects as assigned Minimum\nQualifications: To\nbe considered for the positions, all three of the following qualifications are\nrequired: A doctorate/terminal degree in business or a related field. Past experience in effectively teaching management-related courses at a four-year college or university. A demonstrated record of professional and/or scholarly accomplishment. Preferred\nQualifications: Deep connections to the Chicago Business Community Connection to and familiarity with the UIC Community Application\nInstructions: Please\nread the application instructions below carefully. To Apply ,\nplease complete an online application at \"Apply Now\" and\nupload the required documents that are listed below (please limit your uploads\nto these documents): Curriculum Vita (CV) Cover letter\n     highlighting teaching and other relevant professional experiences Teaching\n     Statement Recent\n     teaching evaluations (or a statement explaining why you don’t have them) Names\n     and contact information for at least three professional references The\nfull link to apply is at: https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20555?c=uic. Please note that once you\nhave submitted your application, you will not be able to make any changes. To\nrevise your application, you must withdraw and reapply. Please ensure the\napplication is fully completed, and all supporting documents have been uploaded\nbefore the posting close date, as you will not be able to reapply after the\nposting close date. Evaluation of\napplications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is\nfilled. If you have questions,\nplease contact Livia Markoczy, Search Committee Chair, at livmarko@uic.edu. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20916?c=uic": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Clinical Anesthesiology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Clinical Anesthesiology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Clinical Anesthesiology Chicago, IL, United States | 1042979 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/21/2026 - Application Deadline: 12/15/2026 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Clinical Anesthesiology Hiring Department : Anesthesiology Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1042979 Salary:  The\nbudgeted salary range for this position is $420,000 to $610,000, based on a\nfull-time equivalent and including additional earnings from participation in\nthe overnight call pool. Salary is competitive and based on qualifications,\nexperience, internal equity, and budget constraints. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary The University of Illinois at Chicago's Department of Anesthesiology is seeking additional Board Certified or Board Eligible Anesthesiologists; subspecialty fellowship training Cardiac, Neurosurgical, Pain Medicine, or Pediatric Anesthesiology is preferred but not required. Duties & Responsibilities Provide anesthesia services. Train residents and fellows. Medically direct CRNAs. Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Board Certified or Board Eligible Anesthesiologist(s). Preferred Qualifications Subspecialty fellowship training in Cardiac, Neurosurgical, or Pediatric Anesthesiology, or Pain Medicine, is preferred but not required.  For Cardiac and Neurosurgical Anesthesiology, a minimum of 3 years of substantial experience is also acceptable. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
