    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/18977?c=uic": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor (Part-time) - UIC Law",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor (Part-time) - UIC Law | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Adjunct Professor (Part-time) - UIC Law Chicago, IL, United States | 1039404 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 2/19/2026 - Application Deadline: 11/9/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Professor (Part-time) - UIC Law Hiring Department : UIC Law Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1039404 Posting Close Date : November 9, 2026 Salary: The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary To support and teach classes in the Law School's Juris Doctor programs. Duties & Responsibilities Develop and deliver engaging and rigorous classroom instruction for the assigned course(s), adhering to the established curriculum and learning objectives. Utilize diverse teaching methods (e.g., lectures, case studies, simulations) to foster active learning and critical thinking among students. Prepare and distribute clear and concise course materials, including syllabi, assignments, and exams. Evaluate student performance through assignments, exams, and participation, providing timely and constructive feedback. Stay current on relevant legal developments and scholarship in the assigned area of law. Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Juris Doctor (JD) degree from an ABA-accredited law school or its equivalent from a foreign country. Minimum of 5 years of experience practicing law in the relevant legal field. Demonstrated ability or potential to teach effectively in a law school setting. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Experience with or willingness to learn the Blackboard learning management system. Admission to a state or foreign bar (or inactive/retired status). Must be in good standing with any bar which they have been admitted. The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour. For fullest consideration, apply online https://jobs.uic.edu by the listed closing date, November 9, 2026. To be considered for an adjunct faculty position, candidates should submit an online application, including a PDF copy of a resume or curriculum vitae; names and contact information (preferably including telephone numbers and email addresses) for three references familiar with the applicant's practice or teaching credentials; and a cover letter or other document identifying the specific courses or programs at the School of Law for which the applicant wishes to be considered. Candidates are asked to refer to the information posted at https://go.uic.edu/lawadjuncts before submitting an application. Specific courses and programs for which the School of Law anticipates hiring adjunct faculty in the near future are posted on that page. Individuals with less than five years of law practice experience who otherwise meet the qualifications for this position should instead consider applying for the Adjunct Teaching Associate position. Offers of employment by the University of Illinois may be subject to approval by the University’s Board of Trustees and are made contingent upon the candidate’s successful completion of any criminal background checks and other pre-employment assessments that may be required for the position being offered. Additional information regarding such pre-employment checks and assessments may be provided as applicable during the hiring process. As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. The University does not engage in discrimination or harassment against any person because of race (ethnicity), color, religion, sex, pregnancy, disability, national origin, citizenship status, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender (including gender identity and gender expression), arrest record status, unfavorable discharge from the military, or status as a protected veteran (military status) and complies with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action laws, orders, and regulations. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21150?c=uic": {
      "title": "Obstetrician and Gynecologist (Open Rank Faculty)",
      "description": "Obstetrician and Gynecologist (Open Rank Faculty) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Obstetrician and Gynecologist (Open Rank Faculty) Chicago, IL, United States | 1042765 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/16/2026 - Application Deadline: 10/30/2026 Back to Search Obstetrician and Gynecologist (Open Rank Faculty) Hiring Department : Obstetrics and Gynecology Location : Chicago, IL Requisition ID : 1042765 Posting Close Date: October 30, 2026 Salary: The budgeted salary range for the position is $220,000 to $240,000. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also considering internal equity. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Illinois Chicago (UIC), in a joint hire with UI Health Mile Square, is seeking a full-time General Obstetrician and Gynecologist (Open Rank Faculty). This position combines clinical service with UI Health's commitment to community health through its FQHC network. The ideal candidate will provide comprehensive obstetric and gynecologic care across various settings, with a specific focus on ambulatory services within the Mile Square health centers. They will participate in the education of medical students and residents and contribute to departmental service and quality improvement initiatives. Faculty are expected to demonstrate a commitment to delivering high-quality, equitable care to a diverse patient population and to support the academic mission of UIC through clinical excellence, teaching, and scholarly activity. Duties & Responsibilities Provide full-scope obstetric and gynecologic care, including outpatient services, inpatient obstetrical care, and gynecologic surgery. Serve as a core provider within the UI Health Mile Square network, dedicating approximately 60% of clinical effort to ambulatory care at the Englewood and Auburn Gresham sites. Provide in-house Labor and Delivery and Obstetrical Emergency Room coverage. Supervise, teach, and mentor medical students, residents, and fellows in clinical and educational settings. Participate in departmental educational activities, including didactic sessions, case conferences, and simulation training. Serve on departmental and institutional committees as nominated by Department leadership. Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Medical Doctor (MD) degree or equivalent. Board certified or board eligible in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Eligible for medical licensure in the State of Illinois. Review of candidates will begin immediately. For fullest consideration, submit CV, cover letter, and names of three references directly on our site. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21145?c=uic": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Tissue Typing/HLA Laboratory; Open Rank Faculty",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Tissue Typing/HLA Laboratory; Open Rank Faculty | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant Director, Tissue Typing/HLA Laboratory; Open Rank Faculty Chicago, IL, United States | 1043363 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/15/2026 - Application Deadline: 12/18/2026 Back to Search Assistant Director, Tissue Typing/HLA Laboratory; Open Rank Faculty Hiring\nDepartment: Pathology Location: Chicago, IL USA Requisition\nID: 1043363 Posting\nClose Date: For\nfullest consideration, please submit a curriculum vitae and names of three\nreferences by December 18, 2026. Salary: The budgeted salary range for the\nposition is $180,000 to $350,000. Salary is competitive and commensurate with\nqualifications and experience, while also considering internal equity. About the\nUniversity of Illinois Chicago UIC is among\nthe nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH\nresearch institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over\n34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the\nnation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian\nAmerican and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and\na Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI). Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces\nnationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs\nin concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a\nfull complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and\ntransformational research along with a commitment to the success of all\nstudents, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university.\nRecent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report,\nfound UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and\namong all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni and is one of the\nlargest employers in the city of Chicago. This\nposition is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a\nRetirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and\ndependents. Position\nSummary The Department of Pathology and Laboratory\nMedicine at the University of Illinois College of Medicine in\nChicago seeks outstanding candidates for a faculty position at the rank of\nAssistant Professor or Associate Professor (rank/tenure commensurate with\nexperience) in Tissue Typing/HLA Laboratory Testing. UI Health is\nan enterprise that includes a 470 bed tertiary care hospital, 30+ outpatient\nclinics and patient-centered research entities including the University of\nIllinois Cancer Center. The University of Illinois College of Medicine Chicago\nis one of three campuses that make up one of the nation’s largest public\nmedical schools. The Department of Pathology in the College of Medicine\nprovides testing in all major disciplines including microbiology, chemistry,\nhematology, transfusion medicine, tissue typing/transplant and molecular\npathology along with surgical pathology and cytopathology services.  UI Health has very active solid organ and\nhematopoietic clinical transplantation programs including liver, renal, small\nbowel, pancreas and hematopoietic progenitor cell transplant. The HLA Laboratory\nis a state of the art newly remodeled laboratory that performs all transplant\nrelated testing in-house. The\nDepartment of Pathology offers a collaborative work environment and provides\nall faculty with professional development opportunities to advance in their\ncareers. Duties\n& Responsibilities This faculty\nposition will be responsible for (1) oversight and performance of a combination\nof HLA/Tissue Typing diagnostic services (2) participating in teaching medical\nstudents, residents, fellows, and house staff and (3) developing or continuing\na basic or translational research program. Professional duties include\ntechnical oversight for immunogenetics and histocompatibility testing in a CAP\naccredited, CLIA regulated clinical laboratory, review and sign out of test\nresults, clinical consultation, virtual crossmatches, monitoring compliance\nwith the Quality Control Plan, test development, validation and implementation.\nParticipation in teaching, administrative work, research and attendance at professional\ndevelopment and scientific meetings is expected. Minimum\nQualifications •              PhD, MD, DO, DO/PhD or MD/PhD\ndegree from an accredited institution •              MD/DO candidates must be Board\ncertified in anatomic and clinical pathology (AP/CP) or clinical pathology (CP) •              MD/DO and PhD candidates must\neither hold certification as a Laboratory Director, Clinical Consultant, and\nTechnical Supervisor for Hematopoietic Stem Cell/Bone Marrow Transplantation\n(Related and Unrelated Donors), and Solid Organ Transplantation (Live Donors)\nby the American College of Histocompatibility and Immunogenetics (ACHI) OR have\ncompleted the Director in Training program and be eligible to take the ACHI Lab\nDirector exam and portfolio presentation (board eligible). The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20941?c=uic": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist, Wood Street Pharmacy",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist, Wood Street Pharmacy | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist, Wood Street Pharmacy Chicago, IL, United States | 1043045 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/15/2026 - Application Deadline: 11/14/2026 Back to Search Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist, Wood Street Pharmacy Hiring Department : Pharmacy Practice Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043045 Salary:  The budgeted salary range for the position is $135000 to $160000. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. The Department of Pharmacy Practice at the University of Illinois\nChicago Retzky College of Pharmacy is seeking a Clinical Instructor/Clinical\nPharmacist, Wood Street Pharmacy to join the Ambulatory Pharmacy Services unit. The practice site\nfor this position is located in Wood Street Pharmacy. Our mission is to provide\nquality health services and promote disease prevention to all in the community\nof the UI Health System. Wood Street Pharmacy is a mail order and specialty pharmacy,\nservicing our patients Monday through Friday. Our pharmacy is looking for a\nfull-time team player who possesses strong oral and written communication\nskills, the ability to work independently, and adapts to a changing work\nenvironment. The successful candidate must also possess excellent time\nmanagement and organizational skills and be committed to providing excellent\npatient care. Demonstrated knowledge and experience with USP 797 and 800\ncompliance and standards in a hospital or clinical setting is preferred. The College\nof Pharmacy at UIC, with campuses in Chicago and Rockford, is the #1 college of\npharmacy in the state of Illinois and the #15 college in the US ranked by US\nNews & World Report. More information about the College and Department of\nPharmacy Practice can be found at https://pharmacy.uic.edu and https://dpp.pharmacy.uic.edu This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary: The Department of Pharmacy Practice at the University of Illinois Chicago College of Pharmacy, is seeking a Clinical Faculty/Clinical Pharmacist to join the Ambulatory Care Pharmacy Services unit. The practice site for this position is located in Wood Street Pharmacy.  Our mission is to provide quality health services and promote disease prevention to all in the community of the UI Health System. Wood Street Pharmacy is a closed-door mail out pharmacy, servicing our patients Monday through Friday. Our pharmacy is looking for a full-time team player who possesses strong oral and written communication skills, the ability to work independently, and adapts to a changing work environment. The successful candidate must also possess excellent time management and organizational skills and be committed to providing excellent patient care. Demonstrated knowledge and experience with USP 797 and 800 compliance and standards in a hospital or clinical setting is preferred. Duties & Responsibilities Clinical Instructor academic responsibilities include the provision of\ndidactic instruction and clinical experiential teaching/training in the Retzky\nCollege of Pharmacy’s Doctor of Pharmacy Program and precepting of PGY1 and\nPGY2 residents. Clinical Pharmacist duties include\nworking closely with pharmacy technicians, students, medical staff and patients\nin providing patient-centered clinical pharmacy services. The accurate and efficient review and verification of medication orders, providing patient medication counseling and working with health care providers and patients to resolve any medication issues. Ensuring that all regulatory requirements are met, directing the activities performed by pharmacy technicians, serving as a resource for clinic-based staff for medication-related questions, and assisting with all mail out activities. Minimum Qualifications: Licensed, or eligible for licensure as a professional pharmacist in Illinois as of start date Graduate of an ACPE accredited College of Pharmacy PharmD program Candidate must possess knowledge and skills such that they qualify for a non-tenured clinical faculty position (at the rank of Clinical Instructor) with the Department of Pharmacy Practice at the UIC College of Pharmacy Preferred Qualifications: Three years of prior pharmacy experience Previous pharmacy management experience Demonstrated knowledge and experience with USP 797 and 800 compliance and standards in a hospital or clinical setting Working knowledge of the programs serviced in the pharmacy The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21105?c=uic": {
      "title": "Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Faculty – DrPH Program – Health Policy and Administration",
      "description": "Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Faculty – DrPH Program – Health Policy and Administration | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Faculty – DrPH Program – Health Policy and Administration Chicago, IL, United States | 1043302 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/8/2027 Back to Search Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Faculty – DrPH Program – Health Policy and Administration Hiring Department : Health Policy and Administration Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043302 Salary: The salary range of employees currently\nholding equivalent positions is $95,000 - $175,000 per academic (9-month) year. POSITION SUMMARY The Division of Health Policy and Administration (HPA) at the University of Illinois Chicago (UIC) School of Public Health (SPH) seeks applications for a faculty member at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Clinical Professor for the DrPH Program, beginning Fall 2027. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement\nPlan, Paid time Off, and Tuition Waivers for employees and dependents. About the\nDrPH Program, HPA Division, SPH, and UIC: The Doctor of Public Health (DrPH) in Leadership program explicitly focuses\non strengthening practitioner-student knowledge, skills, and ability to\nunderstand and address the persistent root causes of inequity. We emphasize\nwhole-person, transformational, and action-learning centered pedagogical\napproaches through a cohort-based collective learning approach. The curriculum\nintegrates and assures achievement of learning aligned with the Council on\nEducation in Public Health (CEPH) and UIC DrPH program competencies grounded in\ntransformational leadership. Our courses are delivered in a synchronous\ndistance-based model that is supported by an ever-growing global community of\nstudent-practitioners, faculty, alumni, staff, and strategic partners. The\nDivision of Health Policy and Administration (HPA) at the UIC SPH is an interprofessional, transdisciplinary\ncommunity addressing the underlying structural and social drivers of population\nhealth and disparities. Through mutually reinforcing teaching, research, and\npractice, we analyze, identify, and implement evidence-based solutions across\npolicy, systems, and organizations in Chicago, nationally, and globally.\nAnchored in community and cross-sector partnerships, our work responds to lived\nexperiences and real-world environments to achieve lasting impact. Our expertise—centered\non health disparities and equity—spans policy, law, economics, health services,\nhealthcare administration, and leadership. The UIC School of Public Health is the only Council on\nEducation for Public Health (CEPH) accredited school of public health in\nIllinois. UIC SPH is dedicated to enhancing quality of life by improving public\nhealth and plays a vital role in educating the nation’s public health\nworkforce. UIC SPH consistently ranks among the top 10% of all schools and\nprograms of public health nationally (ranked 22nd nationally in the 2026 U.S.\nNews & World Report). For more than 50 years, UIC SPH has been the state's\nprincipal educator of public health professionals as well as researchers,\nacademic faculty, policymakers, and activists whose work positively affects\nhealth and well-being in communities that are diverse with respect to race,\nethnicity, socioeconomic status, gender, sexual orientation, nationality, and\nreligion. UIC SPH is one of seven health science colleges that comprise UI\nHealth, the only academic public health center in Chicago. UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban\npublic research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the\nlargest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 37,000 students, comprising one\nof the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a\nMinority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American\nPacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving\nInstitution (HSI). Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and\ninternationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with\ncivic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement\nof health sciences colleges. In 2026, UIC was awarded nearly $500 million in\nsponsored research funding, including $208 million from NIH. By emphasizing\ncutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the\nsuccess of all students, UIC embodies a dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban\nuniversity. UIC is ranked #1 in the state of Illinois for social mobility by\nthe Wall Street Journal and top 10 for social mobility nationally according to\nthe U.S. News & World Report. UIC has 366,000 alumni and is one of the\nlargest employers in the city of Chicago. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Terminal degree. A strong record of teaching, practice, and research is expected, commensurate with career stage. APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Applications received by December 1, 2026\nwill receive full consideration; the search will close on January 8, 2027. The\nanticipated start date is August 2027. A completed online application that\nincludes the following attachments is required for consideration: 1. A cover letter that includes an indication\nof which position is preferred (Assistant, Associate, or Full). 2. A curriculum vitae (CV). 3. A recent scholarly writing sample (e.g.,\ndissertation chapter or published peer-reviewed article on which you are the\nsole or primary author). 4. One-page teaching statement specifying\ntraining in pedagogy, teaching experience, and potential courses within the\nschool's DrPH curriculum. 5. Three letters of recommendation (for those\napplying at the assistant professor level) OR contact information for three\nprofessional references (for those applying at the associate or full professor\nlevel). For specific questions about the application\nprocess, please contact HPA Business Manager, Susan Lynch (slynch2@uic.edu). For questions regarding the\nposition, please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Yuka Asada (yasada2@uic.edu). The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21003?c=uic": {
      "title": "Open Rank Tenure/Tenure Track Faculty - Health Policy and Administration",
      "description": "Open Rank Tenure/Tenure Track Faculty - Health Policy and Administration | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Open Rank Tenure/Tenure Track Faculty - Health Policy and Administration Chicago, IL, United States | 1043102 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/8/2027 Back to Search Open Rank Tenure/Tenure Track Faculty - Health Policy and Administration Hiring Department : Health Policy and Administration Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043102 Salary: The salary range of employees\ncurrently holding equivalent positions is $125,000 - $250,000 per academic\n(9-month) year. POSITION SUMMARY The Division of Health Policy and Administration (HPA) at the University\nof Illinois Chicago (UIC) School of Public Health (SPH) seeks to fill up to\nthree full-time tenure-track or tenured faculty positions at the rank of Assistant,\nAssociate, or Full Professor beginning Fall 2027. Associate or Full Professors\nwill be prioritized. We are seeking candidates for these positions with\nexpertise and training in health policy, public health management, population health,\ndecision sciences, health services, health economics, public policy, public\nhealth law, and/or social and behavioral sciences. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life\nInsurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid Time Off, and Tuition Waivers for employees\nand dependents.  The salary range of\nemployees currently holding equivalent positions is $125,000 - $250,000 per\nacademic (9-month) year. About the HPA Division, SPH,\nand UIC: The Division of Health\nPolicy and Administration (HPA) at the UIC SPH is an\ninterprofessional, transdisciplinary community addressing the underlying structural and social\ndrivers of population health and disparities. Through mutually reinforcing\nteaching, research, and practice, we analyze, identify, and implement\nevidence-based solutions across policy, systems, and organizations in Chicago,\nnationally, and globally. Anchored in community and cross-sector partnerships, our work responds to lived experiences and real-world environments\nto achieve lasting impact. Our expertise—centered on health disparities and\nequity—spans policy, law, economics, health services, healthcare\nadministration, and leadership. The UIC School of Public\nHealth is the only Council on\nEducation for Public Health (CEPH) accredited school of public health in\nIllinois. UIC SPH is dedicated to enhancing quality of life by improving public\nhealth and plays a vital role in educating the nation’s public health\nworkforce. UIC SPH consistently ranks among the top 10% of all schools and\nprograms of public health nationally (ranked 22nd nationally in the 2026 U.S.\nNews & World Report). For more than 50 years, UIC SPH has been the state’s\nprincipal educator of public health professionals as well as researchers,\nacademic faculty, policymakers, and activists whose work positively affects\nhealth and well-being in communities that are diverse with respect to race,\nethnicity, socioeconomic status, gender, sexual orientation, nationality, and\nreligion. UIC SPH is one of seven health science colleges that comprise UI\nHealth, the only academic public health center in Chicago. UIC is among the\nnation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH\nresearch institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 37,000\nstudents, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and\nis designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and\nNative American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic\nServing Institution (HSI). Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and\ninternationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with\ncivic, corporate, and community partners worldwide, including a full complement\nof health sciences colleges. In 2026, UIC was awarded nearly $500 million in\nsponsored research funding, including $208 million from NIH. By emphasizing\ncutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the\nsuccess of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban\nuniversity. UIC is ranked #1 in the state of Illinois for social mobility by\nthe Wall Street Journal and top 10 for social mobility nationally according to\nthe U.S. News & World Report. UIC has 366,000 alumni and is one of the\nlargest employers in the city of Chicago. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS PhD, ScD, MD, or related terminal degree. Expertise and training in health policy, public health management, population health, decision sciences, health economics, public policy, public health law, social and behavioral sciences, political science, and/or public health informatics. APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Applications\nreceived by December 18, 2026 will receive full consideration; the search will\nclose on January 8, 2027. The\nanticipated start date is August 2027. A completed online application that\nincludes the following attachments is required for consideration: 1. A one-page cover letter that\nincludes an indication of which position is preferred (Assistant, Associate, or\nFull). 2. A curriculum vitae (CV). 3. For those applying at the\nrank of Assistant Professor ,\na recent scholarly writing sample (e.g., dissertation chapter or published\npeer-reviewed article on which you are the sole or primary author). 4. One-page research statement,\nspecifying plans for extramural research funding. 5. One-page teaching statement\nspecifying training in pedagogy, teaching experience, and potential courses\nwithin the school’s MPH core curriculum or divisional courses. 6. Contact information for\nthree professional references (for those applying at the associate or full\nprofessor level) OR three letters of recommendation (for those applying at the\nassistant professor level). For specific questions about\nthe application process, please contact HPA Business Manager, Susan Lynch (slynch2@uic.edu). For questions regarding the position, please\ncontact the search committee chair, Dr. Sage Kim (skim49@uic.edu). The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20352?c=uic": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty (Open Rank)/Clinical Pharmacist, Clinical Coordinator, Specialty (SPS)",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty (Open Rank)/Clinical Pharmacist, Clinical Coordinator, Specialty (SPS) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Clinical Faculty (Open Rank)/Clinical Pharmacist, Clinical Coordinator, Specialty (SPS) Chicago, IL, United States | 1042071 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 - Application Deadline: 11/11/2026 Back to Search Clinical Faculty (Open Rank)/Clinical Pharmacist, Clinical Coordinator, Specialty (SPS) Hiring Department : Pharmacy Practice Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1042071 Posting Close Date : November 11, 2026 Salary: The budgeted\nsalary range for the position is $135,000-$175,000. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Summary/Description: The University of Illinois Chicago (UIC) Retzky College\nof Pharmacy, Department of Pharmacy Practice is seeking a full time Clinical Faculty\n(Open Rank)/Clinical Pharmacist, Specialty Pharmacy Clinical Coordinator. The Specialty Clinical Coordinator assists and supports the\nDirector of Ambulatory Pharmacy Services in maintaining the specialty pharmacy\nbusiness in accordance with departmental standards, internal and external\nreporting requirements, accreditation standards, and pharmacy laws and\nregulations. The coordinator has the qualifications to perform clinical\noversight for the services provided. The coordinator supports the SPS objective\nto have qualified SPS clinicians accountable to SPS for decisions affecting\npatients. The coordinator oversees the SPS Patient Management Program to ensure\npatient management is in alignment with evidence-based treatment guidelines,\ncreates and optimizes tools and documentation for clinical monitoring and\nevaluates the clinical proficiency of the patient management pharmacists. The Retzky\nCollege of Pharmacy at\nUIC, with campuses in Chicago and Rockford, is the #1 college of pharmacy in\nthe state of Illinois and the #15 college in the US ranked by US News &\nWorld Report. More information about the College and Department of Pharmacy\nPractice can be found at https://pharmacy.uic.edu and https://dpp.pharmacy.uic.edu. Duties: Clinical Faculty\nresponsibilities of the position include the provision of didactic and clinical\nexperiential teaching/training in the College of Pharmacy’s Doctor of Pharmacy\nProgram. In addition, the coordinator is expected to participate in the education\nof PGY1 and PGY2 residents, international pharmacists, and other pharmacy staff\nby serving as a preceptor and role model as defined by the guidelines and\nrequirements of the Department of Pharmacy Practice. Clinical Pharmacist responsibilities include, but are not limited\nto: Provide direct patient care in SPS, in accordance with all policies and procedures, at a high level in accordance with the clinical leadership role. Serve as a clinical content expert through participation in continuing education activities, review and implementation of evidence-based guidelines, reading professional literature, and attending professional meetings, as appropriate. Coordinator\nresponsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provides education, training, and clinical oversight for patient management services. Evaluates and identifies areas to create or optimize patient management services, based on objective criteria, in accordance with evidence-based guidelines. Ensures patient management and documentation are aligned with current evidence-based practice. Maintains, and collaborates on the development of, the Patient Management Program supportive materials including policies, procedures, protocols and collaborative practice agreements. Updates documentation and monitoring templates and standards. Provides guidance to SPS staff regarding patient care management decisions. Collaborates with clinic pharmacists and pharmacists in ambulatory care pharmacies to coordinate patient care activities. Develops quality improvement programs that relate to patient care, measure performance, create action plans, coordinate and execute action plans, and reports progress and results to the Director and the Quality Management Committee. Oversees activities performed by students, externs and residents. Provide, or oversee (as appropriate), onboarding and ongoing disease state and medication training for SPS staff, and document training activities. Collaborate with the SPS team on the identification of new indications and new medications and creation of supportive materials for patient management and monitoring. Optimize electronic medical record and other technologies to support the effective management, monitoring and documentation of patient care activities. Attend, and actively participate in, departmental, college, team, university and UIH committees. Identify, plan and participate in/lead research, or demonstration, grant opportunities for Ambulatory Pharmacy Services. Prepare grant applications for such opportunities. Provide education of nursing staff, medical staff, and other members of the healthcare team. Minimum Qualifications Graduate of an ACPE accredited College of Pharmacy PharmD program Licensed, or eligible for licensure as a professional pharmacist in Illinois Completion of a PGY1 residency or fellowship program, or equivalent experience Candidate must possess knowledge and skills such that they qualify for a non-tenured clinical faculty position with the Department of Pharmacy Practice at the UIC College of Pharmacy Minimum of 3 years post-graduate experience in patient care Strong written and verbal skills Desire to conduct scholarly writing and research Desire to lead, and participate in, the education of learners Preferred Qualifications: Extensive knowledge of specialty pharmacy services Completion of PGY1 residency or fellowship program Active Certified Specialty Pharmacist credential Board Certification in Ambulatory Care; Pharmacotherapy or related specialty preferred Prior experience with didactic, clerkship or resident precepting experience preferred Experience with data analysis and data-driven decision-making The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20029?c=uic": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist, Ambulatory Pharmacy Services",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist, Ambulatory Pharmacy Services | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist, Ambulatory Pharmacy Services Chicago, IL, United States | 1041410 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 - Application Deadline: 10/31/2026 Back to Search Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist, Ambulatory Pharmacy Services Search extended until 10/30/2026 Hiring Department : Pharmacy Practice Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1041410 Posting Close Date :  10/30/2026 Salary: The budgeted\nsalary rate for the position is up to $160,000. Salary is competitive\nand commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also considering\ninternal equity. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Summary/Description: The University of Illinois Chicago (UIC) Retzky College\nof Pharmacy, Department of Pharmacy Practice is seeking a full time Clinical Instructor/Clinical\nPharmacist within Ambulatory Pharmacy Services. The Clinical Instructor/Clinical Pharmacist provides a high level\nof comprehensive pharmaceutical services as defined in the Departmental Mission\nStatement and the Standards of Practice. This position organizes, supervises,\ndirects, and verifies the duties and functions performed by supportive\npersonnel to ensure the provision of accurate, efficient, and appropriate drug\ndistribution services to the patient. This position also provides direct\npatient care activities to ensure safe and effective drug therapy through the\nprovision of clinical services. Further, the person in this position identifies\npotential problems relating to activities and communicates those situations\nand/or solutions to the appropriate managerial personnel. Finally, the person\nin this position educates and/or advises pharmacy students and pharmacy\nresidents/fellows as well as other health care students and residents. The Retzky\nCollege of Pharmacy at\nUIC, with campuses in Chicago and Rockford, is the #1 college of pharmacy in\nthe state of Illinois and the #15 college in the US ranked by US News &\nWorld Report. More information about the College and Department of Pharmacy\nPractice can be found at https://pharmacy.uic.edu and https://dpp.pharmacy.uic.edu Duties: Clinical Instructor responsibilities of the position include the\nprovision of didactic and clinical experiential teaching/training in the\nCollege of Pharmacy’s Doctor of Pharmacy Program. Clinical Pharmacist (supporting ambulatory retail pharmacies) responsibilities include: Processing of orders - prioritize and verify all new medication orders ensuring accuracy and appropriateness. Check accuracy of all medications prior to dispensing. Personnel supervision - directly supervises pharmacy technicians, students, and residents. Quality Assurance - participates in Medication Use Evaluations. Drug Information - provides complete and accurate drug information. Cost containment - drug therapy provided is cost-effective. Direct patient care - anticoagulation monitoring, participation in code team. Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Work arrangement: On-site position is located on the UIC campus. The pharmacist will support all Ambulatory Retail Pharmacies remotely from a centralized worksite. Minimum Qualifications: PharmD degree from an ACPE accredited Doctor of Pharmacy Program. Must be licensed by the State of Illinois as a Pharmacist or eligible for such license by start date. Must possess knowledge and skills to qualify for a non-tenured clinical faculty position within the Department of Pharmacy Practice at the UIC College of Pharmacy. Preferred Qualifications: Prior cleanroom compounding experience preferred. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/18923?c=uic": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Physician",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Physician | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Physician Peoria, IL, United States | 1039300 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/23/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/22/2027 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Physician Search extended through 8/30/2026 Hiring Department : UICOMP-Pediatrics Location :  Peoria, IL USA Requisition ID : 1039300 Posting Close Date : 4/23/2026 Budgeted Salary Range: $249,084 to $351,382\nper year The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria (UICOMP) seeks candidates for\nthe position(s) of Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics\n(Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Physician) in\nthe Department of Pediatrics. About\nthe University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is a regional campus of one\nof the largest public medical schools in the United States. We are known for\nhaving small class sizes and exceptional faculty mentorship. This allows UICOMP\nstudents to excel under a rigorous curriculum. In collaboration with our\nhospitals and clinical partners, UICOMP Faculty members provide care to more\nthan 45,000 patients each year. In addition, they contribute to medical\neducation and training for more than 260 students, and more than 300 physician\nresidents and fellows annually. UICOMP healthcare partners include Jump\nSimulation, a world-class leader in healthcare simulation and innovation, along\nwith OSF Saint Medical Center, OSF Children’s Hospital of Illinois and Carle\nHearth Greater Peoria. UICOMP is also part of a R1 research institute with\ntranslational research focusing on Alzheimer dementia and oncology. Learn\nmore about how the University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is helping\nto transform healthcare here: https://peoria.medicine.uic.edu/ . This\nposition is intended to be eligible for benefits .\nThis includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan,\nPaid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary The Division of Child Development and Rehabilitation at the University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is recruiting a Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Physician with expertise in care for children with neurodevelopmental disabilities. They will participate in inpatient consultation, outpatient assessment and management, and interdisciplinary care for children with neurodevelopmental disabilities. There is ample opportunity for teaching, research, quality improvement, advocacy, and community involvement. Duties & Responsibilities Assessment and management of children with physical disabilities in the outpatient clinic Inpatient consult and follow-up of patients admitted to CHOI with brain injury, spinal cord injury, physical injury. Follow-up of patients at Almost Home Kids, a transition to home program Management of movement disorders such as spasticity, and dystonia. Participation in the Comprehensive Interdisciplinary Cerebral Pasly Program and the Multidisciplinary Spina Bifida Program. Teaching medical students, residents and fellows Community involvement to enhance the lives of children with disabilities and their families Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications M.D or equivalent Board Certification in PM&R Eligible for licensure in Illinois Preferred Qualifications Fellowship in Pediatric Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Board Eligible in Pediatric Physical Medicine and rehabilitation Desire to develop programs for children with neurodevelopmental disabilities in the region. To apply, please\nvisit this job listing on the UIC Job Board at, https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/18923?c=uic , scroll towards the bottom of the page and click, “Apply\nNow”. You may be\nredirected to log into, or to create a new account. For fullest\nconsideration please apply by 6/22/2026. The budgeted salary\nrange for the position is $249,084 to $351,382 per year. Salary is\ncompetitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also\nconsidering internal equity. The\nUniversity of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but\nnot limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all\napplicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required\nEmployment Notices and Posters at https://www.hr.uillinois.edu/cms/one.aspx?portalId=4292&pageId=5705 to view our non-discrimination statement and\nfind additional information about required background checks, sexual\nharassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through\nE-Verify. The\nuniversity provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an\nAccommodation at https://jobs.uic.edu/request-and-accomodation/ Artificial\nIntelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review\nprocess for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a\nperson. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21190?c=uic": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics (Dermatology)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics (Dermatology) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics (Dermatology) Peoria, IL, United States | 1043475 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/17/2027 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics (Dermatology) Hiring Department : UICOMP-Pediatrics Location :  Peoria, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043475 Salary: $345,400 to $468,200 per year The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria (UICOMP) seeks candidates for\nthe position(s) of Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics in the Department\nof Pediatrics (Dermatology). This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. About\nthe University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is a regional campus of one\nof the largest public medical schools in the United States. We are known for\nhaving small class sizes and exceptional faculty mentorship. This allows UICOMP\nstudents to excel under a rigorous curriculum. In collaboration with our\nhospitals and clinical partners, UICOMP Faculty members provide care to more\nthan 45,000 patients each year. In addition, they contribute to medical\neducation and training for more than 260 students, and more than 300 physician\nresidents and fellows annually. UICOMP healthcare partners include Jump\nSimulation, a world-class leader in healthcare simulation and innovation, along\nwith OSF Saint Medical Center, OSF Children’s Hospital of Illinois and Carle\nHearth Greater Peoria. UICOMP is also part of a R1 research institute with\ntranslational research focusing on Alzheimer dementia and oncology. Learn\nmore about how the University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is helping\nto transform healthcare here: https://peoria.medicine.uic.edu/ . Position Summary This Pediatric Dermatologist will provide outpatient services at the Children's Hospital of Illinois and also provide inpatient consultations to the Children's Hospital of Illinois. They will be responsible for teaching medical students and residents. Scholarly work activity (research, quality improvement, and advocacy) is expected but tailored to the faculty member's interests. Duties & Responsibilities Provide Pediatric Dermatology services to patients of the Children’s Hospital of Illinois in an outpatient setting Provide Pediatric Dermatology inpatient consultations to the patients inside the Children’s Hospital of Illinois Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications MD/DO degree Eligible for licensure in Illinois. Board certified in Dermatology 3 years Dermatology Residency 1 year Pediatric Dermatology fellowship To apply, please\nvisit this job listing on the UIC Job Board at, https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21190?c=uic , scroll towards the bottom of the page and click, “Apply\nNow”. You may be\nredirected to log into, or to create a new account. For fullest\nconsideration please apply by 11/9/2026. The budgeted salary\nrange for the position is $345,400\nto $468,200 per year. Salary is\ncompetitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also\nconsidering internal equity. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21057?c=uic": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Synthetic Biology/ Biotechnology- Dept of Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Synthetic Biology/ Biotechnology- Dept of Biological Sciences | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Synthetic Biology/ Biotechnology- Dept of Biological Sciences Chicago, IL, United States | 1043012 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 - Application Deadline: 12/18/2026 Back to Search Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Synthetic Biology/ Biotechnology- Dept of Biological Sciences Hiring Department : Biological Sciences Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043012 Salary: The budgeted salary range for the position is $100,000 to\n$120,000. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and\nexperience, while also considering internal equity. Posting\nClose Date : December\n18, 2026 About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. About\nthe Department of Biological Sciences The\nDepartment of Biological Sciences, which resides in the College of Liberal Arts\nand Sciences, has research strengths in Molecular, Cellular and Developmental\nBiology, Neurobiology, and Ecology and Evolution. The department currently has\n28 tenure-line faculty and 11 non-tenure track faculty, >2400 undergraduate\nmajors and over 105 graduate students. See http://bios.uic.edu/ for more information. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position\nSummary The Department of Biological\nSciences at the University of Illinois Chicago invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor\nposition in Synthetic Biology. We seek creative and innovative candidates who\nuse molecular, genetic, biochemical, structural, computational, and/or cellular\napproaches to study and engineer biological systems. Research interests may span a broad range of\nexperimental platforms and organisms, from in vitro systems, to\nmicroorganisms, plants and animals. Areas of interest are broad and include,\nbut are not limited to, synthetic gene circuits and regulatory networks, genome\nengineering, metabolic engineering, engineered cellular systems, protein and\nRNA engineering, in vitro and\ncell-free systems, protein and macromolecular design, and machine learning and\nAI driven approaches. We are particularly interested in research that applies\nour understanding of fundamental biological processes to the design of new\nbiological systems and functions, including the engineering of gene expression,\nprotein synthesis, and the production of biomolecules with novel properties.\nAll scales of analysis and research will be considered. Researchers working in\nthe field of synthetic biology and using approaches to tackle evolutionary\nquestions that connect with Departmental strengths in ecology and evolution,\nmolecular, cell and developmental biology, and neurobiology, are encouraged to\napply. The successful candidate will\nbe expected to establish a vigorous, independent research program supported by\nexternal funding and demonstrate a commitment to excellence in the graduate and\nundergraduate teaching and mentoring. Duties & Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, active, and externally funded research program utilizing any combination of experimental and computational approaches to rationally design and/or synthesize new biological molecules, pathways, or systems with the goal of advancing novel technologies or elucidating foundational principles in biology. Participate in the intellectual life of the university. Seek external funding in support of their research program. Teach biochemistry or related topics to UIC undergraduate and graduate students in Biological Sciences. Guide students in research. Provide service to the Department and University in the form of committee work, seminar coordination, policy review, and/or mentorship and other service activities. Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum\nQualifications: The\ncandidate must have a PhD degree or equivalent doctoral degree in relevant\ndiscipline, have relevant postdoctoral or equivalent research experience, and\ndemonstrate a strong record of research accomplishments. For\nfull consideration, please complete an online application and\nsubmit the following materials: - Cover letter outlining applicant qualifications and motivation - Curriculum vitae - Research plan (up to 3 pages) - Teaching philosophy statement (1 page) - Names\nand contact information (including email addresses) for at least 3 references Applications\nshould be submitted by December 18, 2026. Review of applications will\nbegin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Final\nauthorization of the position is subject to availability of funding. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20318?c=uic": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Cardiology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Cardiology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Cardiology Peoria, IL, United States | 1041975 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/18/2027 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Cardiology Search Extended to 1/18/27 Hiring Department : UICOMP-Pediatrics Location :  Peoria, IL USA Requisition ID : 1041975 Posting Close Date : 10/5/2026 Salary: $230,000 to $313,933 per year The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria (UICOMP) seeks candidates for\nthe position of Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical\nPediatrics-Cardiology in the Department\nof Pediatrics. About\nthe University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is a regional campus of one\nof the largest public medical schools in the United States. We are known for\nhaving small class sizes and exceptional faculty mentorship. This allows UICOMP\nstudents to excel under a rigorous curriculum. In collaboration with our\nhospitals and clinical partners, UICOMP Faculty members provide care to more\nthan 45,000 patients each year. In addition, they contribute to medical\neducation and training for more than 260 students, and more than 300 physician\nresidents and fellows annually. UICOMP healthcare partners include Jump\nSimulation, a world-class leader in healthcare simulation and innovation, along\nwith OSF Saint Medical Center, OSF Children’s Hospital of Illinois and Carle\nHearth Greater Peoria. UICOMP is also part of a R1 research institute with\ntranslational research focusing on Alzheimer dementia and oncology. Learn\nmore about how the University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is helping\nto transform healthcare here: https://peoria.medicine.uic.edu/ . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary The Department of Pediatrics of the University of Illinois College of Medicine at Peoria (UICOMP) seeks Fetal & Pediatric Echocardiology candidates for a pediatric cardiology faculty position. Duties & Responsibilities Patient care duties including inpatient, outpatient and echocardiography Satellite clinics in the region On-call duties for pediatric & congenital cardiology Teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows Academic efforts including original research and QI Imaging QI for Echo Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications MD/DO or foreign equivalent Eligible for licensure in Illinois BC/BE in Pediatric Cardiology 3 years pediatric residency/3years pediatric cardiology fellowship or equivalent Significant experience or formal training in Pediatric & Fetal Echocardiography Pediatric and congenital transesophageal echocardiography To apply, please\nvisit this job listing on the UIC Job Board at, https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20318?c=uic , scroll towards the bottom of the page and click, “Apply\nNow”. You may be\nredirected to log into, or to create a new account. For fullest\nconsideration please apply by 11/10/2026. The budgeted salary\nrange for the position is $230,000 to $313,933 per year. Salary is\ncompetitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also\nconsidering internal equity. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
