    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21164?c=uic": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty (Open Rank)/ Clinical Pharmacist, Oncology",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty (Open Rank)/ Clinical Pharmacist, Oncology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Clinical Faculty (Open Rank)/ Clinical Pharmacist, Oncology Chicago, IL, United States | 1043435 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/28/2026 - Application Deadline: 11/20/2026 Back to Search Clinical Faculty (Open Rank)/ Clinical Pharmacist, Oncology, Retzky College of Pharmacy, Department of Pharmacy Practice Hiring Department: Pharmacy Practice Location: Chicago Requisition ID: 1043435 Posting Close Date: Friday, November 20, 2026 Salary: The budgeted salary rate for this position is $146,000 - $185,000. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also considering internal equity. About the University of Illinois Chicago Retzky College of Pharmacy The\nUIC Retzky College of Pharmacy, Department of Pharmacy Practice, is seeking a full-time,\nmotivated professional for the position of Clinical Faculty (Open\nRank)/Clinical Pharmacist who will be assigned to UI Health’s Hematology/Oncology\nservices. The\nideal candidate will be responsible for providing pharmaceutical care to\npatients in the areas of hematology and oncology, both in the hospital and at on-site\nclinics at the University of Illinois Hospital.  The hospital is a 450-bed academic institution located approximately 2\nmiles west of downtown Chicago. The hospital serves an urban, indigent patient\npopulation. It\nis among a select group of medical centers accredited by the Commission on\nCancer. Cancer services at UI Health are comprised of several programs\ncommitted to diagnosing and treating common and rare cancers, including breast,\ncolorectal, gynecologic, head & neck, hematologic/blood, lung, and other cancers. The Retzky College of Pharmacy, with campuses in Chicago and Rockford, is the\n#1 college of pharmacy in the state of Illinois and #6 in total research grant\nfunding, according to the American Association of Colleges of Pharmacy (AACP).\nMore information about the College and Department of Pharmacy Practice can be\nfound at https://pharmacy.uic.edu and https://dpp.pharmacy.uic.edu. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Duties: The hematology and oncology clinical\npharmacist team will consist of 7 pharmacists who are integral members of the hospital's\nand clinics' multidisciplinary teams. The Clinical Pharmacist's duties include\nmedication review and reconciliation, medication selection and dosing\nrecommendations, TPN management, immunosuppression and infectious disease\nprophylaxis selection, management of nausea and pain, therapeutic drug\nmonitoring, provision of drug information, and patient education. The candidate\nwill also be responsible for nurse, physician, and pharmacy staff development;\ncoordinating and conducting quality improvement projects; and developing\ncollaborative treatment and research protocols. The academic\nresponsibilities of the clinical faculty member (Clinical\nAssistant/Associate/Full Professor) include the provision of didactic\nlectures and precepting entry-level Doctor of Pharmacy students, PGY1 residents,\nand PGY2 residents. Scholarly activities, including presentations and\npublications, are an expectation as well. Qualifications: PharmD and PGY1 residency experience required. PGY2 residency in Oncology, or 2-3 years of equivalent clinical experience as a clinical pharmacist in hematology and oncology, is required. Candidates must present evidence of, or eligibility for, Illinois licensure as a professional pharmacist at time of employment. Highly preferred: strong clinical knowledge base; analytical and problem-solving skills; strong verbal and written communication skills; ability to consistently meet deadlines; demonstrate flexibility and ability to work independently and adapt to a changing work environment; excellent planning, time management, and organizational skills. Academic rank commensurate with experience. For fullest consideration, submit a completed application by the close date.  A letter of intent, current curriculum vitae, and the names and email addresses of three professional references must be attached to the application. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21250?c=uic": {
      "title": "Associate/Professor Pediatric Cardiology/Section Chief",
      "description": "Associate/Professor Pediatric Cardiology/Section Chief | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Associate/Professor Pediatric Cardiology/Section Chief Peoria, IL, United States | 1043477 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/25/2027 Back to Search Associate/Professor Pediatric Cardiology/Section Chief Hiring Department : UICOMP-Pediatrics Location :  Peoria, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043477 Salary: $400,000 to $600,000 per year The University\nof Illinois College of Medicine Peoria (UICOMP) seeks candidates for the\nposition(s) of Associate/Professor\nPediatric Cardiology/Section Chief in\nthe Department of Pediatrics About\nthe University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is a regional campus of one\nof the largest public medical schools in the United States. We are known for\nhaving small class sizes and exceptional faculty mentorship. This allows UICOMP\nstudents to excel under a rigorous curriculum. In collaboration with our\nhospitals and clinical partners, UICOMP Faculty members provide care to more\nthan 45,000 patients each year. In addition, they contribute to medical\neducation and training for more than 260 students, and more than 300 physician\nresidents and fellows annually. UICOMP healthcare partners include Jump\nSimulation, a world-class leader in healthcare simulation and innovation, along\nwith OSF Saint Medical Center, OSF Children’s Hospital of Illinois and Carle\nHearth Greater Peoria. UICOMP is also part of a R1 research institute with\ntranslational research focusing on Alzheimer dementia and oncology. Learn\nmore about how the University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is helping\nto transform healthcare here: https://peoria.medicine.uic.edu/ . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary The Department of Pediatrics of the University of Illinois\nCollege of Medicine Peoria (UICOMP) seeks a nationally recognized Pediatric\nCardiologist with a strong track record of leadership and of building clinical\nprograms. There is an expectation that the new leader will grow the current\nclinical programs and develop a strategy to promote destination program status\nand regional referrals. The Section currently offers opportunities to\nparticipate in medical student, resident, and fellow education. The new leader\nwill ensure the section continues to contribute to the education mission of the\ndepartment and hospital. University and Health system leaders will consider\nsupporting the development of fellowship training programs to promote the\nprogram's regional and national reputation. The leader will promote the growth\nof clinical and translational research with emphasis on institution wide\ncollaboration. It is expected that the new Section Chief will develop and\nsubmit a research strategy for the section within the first year and align it\nwith the Department and Children's Hospital of Illinois research and innovation\npriorities. The new leader will enhance clinical operations with the goal to\ngrow and expand current clinical offerings and align clinical research\npriorities to enhance the program stature as a regional and national leader.\nThe Section Chief must exhibit the qualities required to be a successful leader\nin a complex organization, including working collaboratively across various\norganizations and effectively promoting the Section with community providers,\nleaders, donors, and hospital executives. This individual will have the\nopportunity to work in a blended academic/not-for-profit hospital with some\nverticals that are within private practice (i.e. Anesthesia/CIRA). Duties & Responsibilities The\n     Section of Pediatric Cardiology consists of 10 physicians, 4 Advanced Practice\n     Providers. There are two pediatric intervention cardiologists, two board\n     certified ACHD physicians, three fetal cardiologists, an advanced imaging\n     cardiologist, and a preventive cardiologist. The\n     cardiac cath lab provides state-of-the-art interventions for children and\n     adults with congenital heart disease. Bolstered by 2 trained\n     Interventional Cardiologists, the lab offers care to tiny premature\n     infants all the way to adults with congenital heart disease. The annual volume\n     has grown to nearly 200 cases. The cath lab equipment is slated to be\n     upgraded in the next year and this position will move into a new pediatric\n     spirality center opening early 2028. Adult\n     Congenital Cardiology is a program through the Congenital Heart Center and\n     reports through the division of pediatric cardiology. The ACHD program is\n     a regional leader and has ACHA accreditation for nearly 10 years. The\n     program sees the most complex ACHD patients, and teams with interventional\n     cardiology, EP, cardiac surgery, heart failure, transplant, MFM, and\n     anesthesia to provide outstanding care. The team consists of two boarded\n     ACHD physicians, two trained APRNs, a nurse coordinator, and a social\n     worker. Our\n     echocardiography program is IAC certified in pediatric/congenital\n     transthoracic, fetal, and transesophageal echo. The fetal echo team is a\n     member of the Fetal Heart Society and has collaboration with the\n     Perinatology team through the Fetal Care Center. Nearly 1000 fetal echocardiograms\n     are performed every year and total TTE volume is over 6000 per year.\n     Additionally, remote surface echo reads are provided for nearly 20 other\n     facilities. The echo lab team has a robust QI program supported by\n     pediatric dedicated sonographers. Advanced\n     cardiac imaging is outstanding at our institution.  Cardiac MRI and\n     CT are supported through a joint effort between cardiology and\n     radiology.  This collaboration brings high-quality imaging to support\n     the surgical team as well as procedural planning. Advanced imaging\n     techniques such as 3D rendering and 4D beating hearts are frequently\n     utilized to better delineate complex anatomy. There\n     is an active Pediatric & Congenital Cardiovascular surgical program at\n     our center.  This program is the only such program in downstate\n     Illinois and has been in operation for over 45 years.  The team is\n     led by two cardiovascular surgeons that partner with the cardiologists to\n     provide outstanding care. There\n     is a strong Pediatric Critical Care program with 16 critical care beds,\n     and an open intermediate care 16 beds. The Critical care service cares for\n     about 1900 patients per year, more than one third are from regional\n     transport.  The system has active air and ground transport programs.\n     Cardiac Critical Care is directed by dually boarded critical care and\n     cardiology physicians.  Provides support for the congenital heart\n     surgical program, an active diagnostic/Interventional Cardiology program,\n     and patients with other cardiac conditions. A multidisciplinary program\n     provides support for the certified ECMO program. The\n     Neonatal Intensive Care unit consists of a 60-bed unit.  The NICU is\n     the highest designated level by the state of Illinois and provides care\n     for the most premature and complex neonates.  ECMO service is\n     provided.  Interventional cardiology provides PDA occlusion devices\n     for premature infants.  Pre-operative neonates are cared for in a\n     collaborative manner with neonatology, cardiology and cardiac\n     surgery. Additional\n     clinical programs are robust and well supported.  These include\n     Cardiac Neurodevelopmental follow up, Down Syndrome clinic, satellite\n     clinics, and the Pediatric Lipid clinic. One\n     successful research and innovation program in the section is the Advanced\n     Imaging and Modeling lab.  This partnership between the section,\n     department, and hospital allows for the team of imaging cardiology and\n     engineering to build state of the art imaging techniques.  This lab\n     has developed numerous patents and is now incorporating AI into the\n     cardiac imaging repertoire. Department of Pediatrics: The\n     Department of Pediatrics is one of the largest departments at UICOMP. In\n     collaboration with the OSF HealthCare Children’s Hospital of Illinois, the\n     Department has 19 sections and over 145 faculty members providing general\n     pediatrics and subspecialty services to the pediatric population in Central Illinois.\n     The Research office with research coordinators, biostatisticians and\n     epidemiologist support the faculty in the department. Grant writing and\n     research mentorship support is also available. The department has identified understanding how prenatal,\n     neonatal, and childhood exposures influence lifelong health outcomes as\n     the research focus. Department supports up to $200k of internal pilot\n     research grants per year and Children’s Hospital of Illinois provides additional $100k of grant\n     funding. There is a well-developed research core with expertise in machine\n     learning and artificial intelligence research. This group has developed a\n     strong collaboration with Center for Health Research at:\n     https://peoria.medicine.uic.edu/uicomp-research/center-4-health-research/\n     and Department of Biomedical and Health Information Sciences at the University\n     of Illinois Chicago at: https://hds.uic.edu/. The department is currently participating in several Epic Cosmos studies. The\n     Pediatric and Med-Peds Residency program has more than 75 residents who\n     rotate through pediatric inpatient and ambulatory programs including\n     Pediatric Cardiology. We also offer pediatric hospital medicine, critical\n     care, neonatology and gastroenterology fellowships. University of Illinois College of\n     Medicine, Peoria is one of the regional campuses and accepts up to 55\n     medical students every year who rotate through Children’s Hospital of\n     Illinois for their training and several department faculty serve in leadership roles in medical education. Pediatric Cardiology and Jump Simulation Collaboration: Jump\n     Simulation and Trading Center is a collaboration between UICOMP and OSF\n     HealthCare. The center replicates a variety of patient care settings to\n     ensure novice and seasoned clinicians can practice handling medical situations\n     in a lifelike environment. Jump Advanced Imaging and Modeling, created in 2013, is a\n     collaborative effort between engineers and medical professionals to\n     perfect the vision of human anatomy and pathology through 3D/4D modeling\n     and imaging. The National Institutes of Health 3D Print Exchange Heart Library, curated by\n     the Jump Trading Simulation & Education Center, was developed to\n     promote the understanding of congenital heart disease through the open\n     sharing of hearts and ideas. There are several ongoing collaborations with Jump Innovation and the\n     Department in simulation, advanced imaging, artificial intelligence and\n     machine learning application in healthcare research. The\n     primary teaching hospital of UICOMP is Children’s Hospital of Illinois, a\n     tertiary care facility serving a 37-county region with a population base\n     of over two million. Children’s Hospital of Illinois provides\n     comprehensive services to children, including Level IV NICU and a state-designated Pediatric Critical Care\n     Center. Children’s Hospital of Illinois is a major medical facility with\n     136 beds and a 32-bed critical care unit and the only Level 1 trauma\n     center in Illinois outside of Chicago. There are existing resources through UICOMP and Children’s\n     Hospital of Illinois for seeding research funding, quality and outcomes\n     focused academic work and innovation in health education. The\n     Section is actively engaged in quality improvement and process improvement\n     research. Last year the Section published manuscripts, case reports,\n     presented at national conferences, and invited lecturers. The\n     Section Chief will lead the section faculty and advanced practice\n     providers in: Advocating\n     and promoting the care of children with acute and chronic cardiac\n     disorders and adult patients born with congenital heart defects. Providing\n     consultation and support to other services regarding assessment and stabilization\n     of children with cardiac abnormalities in the hospital and across Central\n     Illinois. Providing\n     consultation services for physicians and patients in the region with\n     cardiac diseases and overseeing the regional expansion of cardiology\n     programs and services. Collaborating\n     with the pediatric and congenital cardiothoracic surgery team, anesthesia\n     and cardiac critical care physicians to develop care pathways to ensure\n     coordinated and high-quality care for children undergoing surgery for congenital\n     heart defects and other disorders. Collaborating\n     with nursing leadership, echosonography, Cardiac Cath lab team, radiology,\n     and other ancillary services to provide high quality, safe, and\n     individualized patient and family centered care. Sustaining\n     the existing supportive and collaborative environment for other\n     subspecialists thus facilitating programs that care for high complexity\n     patients. Supporting\n     quality improvement efforts and safety initiatives within pediatric\n     cardiology and cardiac surgery program. Work\n     closely with the Children’s Hospital CMO and Director of Quality and\n     Safety to ensure program outcomes and quality meet the national peer\n     benchmarks. Supporting undergraduate,\n     graduate and continuing education programs of the Department. Work closely\n     with the Pediatric Critical Care Fellowship Program Director to\n     support and strengthen the critical care fellowship program, andoversee\n     the faculty’s contribution to nursing, APPs, and transport team education. Developing a clinical\n     research and innovation strategy for the section in collaboration with the\n     Pediatric Cardiothoracic Surgery team and aligning it with the\n     Children’s Hospital of Illinois destination program development strategy.\n     Promoting research grant funding within the section to sustain the\n     research infrastructure. Performing the duties of a\n     university faculty member including committee assignments, curriculum\n     development and administration. Minimum Qualifications MD/DO degree Completed both Pediatric residency and Pediatric Cardiology fellowship training Minimum of 6 years of Pediatric Cardiology experience Board Certified in Pediatric Cardiology Eligible for licensure in Illinois Preferred Qualifications Leadership experience in pediatric cardiology To apply, please\nvisit this job listing on the UIC Job Board at, https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21250?c=uic , scroll towards the bottom of the page and click, “Apply Now”. You may be\nredirected to log into, or to create a new account. For fullest\nconsideration please apply by 11/16/2026. The budgeted salary\nrange for the position is $400,000 to $600,000 per year. Salary is\ncompetitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also\nconsidering internal equity. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21248?c=uic": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Infectious Disease",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Infectious Disease | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Infectious Disease Peoria, IL, United States | 1043572 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/25/2027 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Infectious Disease Hiring Department : UICOMP-Pediatrics Location :  Peoria, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043572 Salary: $168,000 to $217,000 per year The University\nof Illinois College of Medicine Peoria (UICOMP) seeks candidates for the\nposition(s) of Assistant/Associate/Professor of Clinical Pediatrics-Infectious\nDisease in the Department of Pediatrics About\nthe University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is a regional campus of one\nof the largest public medical schools in the United States. We are known for\nhaving small class sizes and exceptional faculty mentorship. This allows UICOMP\nstudents to excel under a rigorous curriculum. In collaboration with our\nhospitals and clinical partners, UICOMP Faculty members provide care to more\nthan 45,000 patients each year. In addition, they contribute to medical\neducation and training for more than 260 students, and more than 300 physician\nresidents and fellows annually. UICOMP healthcare partners include Jump\nSimulation, a world-class leader in healthcare simulation and innovation, along\nwith OSF Saint Medical Center, OSF Children’s Hospital of Illinois and Carle\nHearth Greater Peoria. UICOMP is also part of a R1 research institute with\ntranslational research focusing on Alzheimer dementia and oncology. Learn\nmore about how the University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is helping\nto transform healthcare here: https://peoria.medicine.uic.edu/ . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary Provide clinical care to patients admitted to Children's Hospital of Illinois and associated ambulatory clinics. Participate in teaching medical students and residents, and scholarly activities. Duties & Responsibilities Provide clinical services (inpatient and outpatient). Participate in teaching medical students, residents, and other health professionals. Conduct clinical and/or translational research in the field of Pediatric Infectious Disease. Participate in infection prevention and antibiotic stewardship committees. Provide phone consultations for other hospitals and Pediatric offices in Illinois. Provide guidance for community outbreaks (ie: measles and tuberculosis). This a faculty position which requires clinical care, teaching medical students and residents, research, and scholarly activities. Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent foreign medical degree Completion of an ACGME-accredited pediatric residency Completion of an ACGME-accredited pediatric infectious diseases fellowship, or expected completion by the start date Board certified or board eligible in General Pediatrics (ABP or AOBP) Board eligible in Pediatric Infectious Diseases, with certification obtained within the ABP eligibility window Eligible for an unrestricted Illinois medical license and Illinois controlled substance license by the start date Eligible for DEA registration Eligible for medical staff privileges at OSF Saint Francis Medical Center and payer credentialing International medical graduates: current ECFMG certification BLS and PALS certification by the start date Preferred Qualifications Scholarly productivity during training, such as first-author publications, abstracts, or manuscripts in preparation A fellowship research or quality improvement project with a clear path to continued work Interest or training in antimicrobial stewardship or hospital epidemiology (for example, SIDP or MAD-ID stewardship certificate, SHEA training) Interest in a focus area that complements the division, such as immunocompromised host ID, congenital infections, vaccines, or EHR-based outcomes research Teaching experience with residents and medical students Plans for academic development, such as a career development award or advanced degree (MPH, MS in clinical research) Strong communication skills and a collaborative approach with hospitalist, critical care, neonatal, oncology, and surgical teams Bilingual ability or experience caring for diverse and rural populations To apply, please\nvisit this job listing on the UIC Job Board at, https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21248?c=uic , scroll towards the bottom of the page and click, “Apply\nNow”. You may be\nredirected to log into, or to create a new account. For fullest\nconsideration please apply by 11/16/2026. The budgeted salary\nrange for the position is $168,000 to $217,000 per year. Salary is\ncompetitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also\nconsidering internal equity. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21147?c=uic": {
      "title": "Division Director and Professor - Epidemiology and Biostatistics",
      "description": "Division Director and Professor - Epidemiology and Biostatistics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Division Director and Professor - Epidemiology and Biostatistics Chicago, IL, United States | 1043355 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/23/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/8/2027 Back to Search Division Director and Professor - Epidemiology and Biostatistics Hiring Department : Epidemiology and Biostatistics Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043355 Salary: The budgeted salary range for this position is\n$180,000 to $240,000 (9-month service basis). The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on\nfactors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the\nselected candidate including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or\ndiscipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary The University of Illinois Chicago (UIC) seeks\napplications for the position of Director of the Division of Epidemiology and\nBiostatistics in the School of Public Health (SPH). We seek a visionary and strategic leader who\nwill champion a culture of scholarly excellence, collaboration, and public\nhealth impact. The Director will support faculty, staff, and students while\nadvancing the Division's mission through impactful research, exceptional\neducational programs, and meaningful engagement with communities and partners\nacross the public health landscape. The successful candidate will possess demonstrated leadership experience, a\nnational and international reputation for scholarly excellence, and a strong\nscientific foundation in epidemiology, biostatistics, or both. The ideal\ncandidate will have strong methodologic expertise and a proven record of\ninterdisciplinary collaboration between epidemiology and biostatistics. We\nwelcome applicants with research interests spanning biostatistical methods and\nepidemiology, including analytical, computational, and population-based\napproaches to understanding the determinants, prevention, and outcomes of\nhealth and disease. Candidates must maintain an active, externally funded\nresearch program and a record of scholarship commensurate with appointment at\nthe rank of Professor with tenure. Additional desired qualifications include\noutstanding communication, faculty mentorship, team-building, and\nadministrative skills; a demonstrated commitment to advancing public health\nresearch and practice; and an entrepreneurial approach to fostering innovation,\ncollaboration, and growth within the Division. The Division of Epidemiology and Biostatistics is a nationally recognized\nacademic unit committed to improving population health through innovative\nresearch, interdisciplinary collaboration, and excellence in education. Our faculty engage in diverse and impactful research that spans public health, clinical,\nand quantitative disciplines. Faculty research areas include: (in\nBiostatistics) Bayesian modeling and inference, causal inference, longitudinal\nand clustered data, cancer clinical trials and data modeling, survival\nanalysis, high dimensional data analysis, mediation analysis, EHR data, and\nneuroimaging data; and (in Epidemiology) chronic diseases, infectious diseases,\ncancer, environmental and occupational health epidemiology, maternal and child\nhealth and global health. The Division offers a comprehensive portfolio of\ngraduate degree programs, including the Master of Public Health (MPH), Master\nof Science (MS), and Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) degrees in Epidemiology and\nBiostatistics, preparing the next generation of public health leaders,\nresearchers, and quantitative scientists through advanced training in study\ndesign, statistical methods, data analysis, and translational public health\nresearch. Duties & Responsibilities - Providing leadership and vision to the division, setting strategic priorities and advancing the goals of the mission in research, teaching, service and outreach activities. - Developing and communicating the division’s policy guidelines in consultation with the faculty. - Supporting the division’s educational mission and promoting student professional development. - Mentoring and facilitating the career advancement of faculty, staff, and students in the division. - Promoting a collaborative environment that fosters success through strong leadership and shared governance. - Managing the division’s budget, resources and personnel for the maximal benefit of the division and school. - Providing leadership, with school support, for development and fundraising activities. - Representing the division at the school and university levels. - Facilitating partnerships with the stakeholders of the division, including leaders in industry, government, other universities, public groups, and professional societies. - Collaborating with School of Public Health's (SPH) director of marketing and communications, developing a proactive recruitment and marketing campaign for the division. - Serving as a member of the SPH leadership team, engaging in meaningful discussions with the dean, senior associate dean and associate deans concerning division priorities, School level funding initiatives and inter or transdisciplinary efforts intended to advance the missions of the division, school, and university. Minimum Qualifications Doctoral degree or equivalent terminal degree Demonstrated academic and research leadership experience, including faculty mentoring Demonstrated supervisory experience Application\nInformation and Instructions Applications received by December 18, 2026 will receive full consideration; the\nsearch will close on January 8, 2027. The anticipated start date for this\nposition is August 2027. A completed online application that includes the\nfollowing attachments is required for consideration: 1. A cover letter specifying qualifications for the role. 2. A curriculum vitae (CV). 3. One-page research statement, specifying current and future plans for extramural research funding. 4. Contact information for three professional references. For specific\nquestions about the application process, please contact Kamil Czarnowski (kczarn4@uic.edu). For questions regarding the\nposition, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Kristen Malecki (kmalecki@uic.edu). To learn more about the Division of Epidemiology and Biostatistics and the School of Public Health, please visit: https://publichealth.uic.edu/. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21056?c=uic": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cell Biology- Department of Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cell Biology- Department of Biological Sciences | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cell Biology- Department of Biological Sciences Chicago, IL, United States | 1043009 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/21/2026 - Application Deadline: 12/19/2026 Back to Search Tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cell Biology- Department of Biological Sciences Hiring Department : Biological Sciences Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043009 Salary: The budgeted salary range for the position is $100,000 to $120,000. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also considering internal equity. Posting Close Date: December 18, 2026 UIC faculty are expected to carry out their responsibilities in person and onsite as part of a vibrant and collegial on-campus community. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits. This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement plan, Paid time off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. About the Department of Biological Sciences The Department of Biological Sciences, part of the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences, offers the largest and fastest-growing major in the college. The department currently has 28 tenure-line faculty and 11 non-tenure-track faculty, > 2,400 undergraduate majors and over 105 graduate students, and is committed to continued hiring of outstanding new faculty. Faculty members have broad research interests, with strengths in neurobiology, cell biology, developmental biology, and genetics, utilizing a diverse array of model organisms. The Department fosters a vibrant, collaborative community, partnering with institutions like the University of Chicago, Northwestern University, Rush Medical College, the Chicago Field Museum, and other local organizations. Recruitment includes a generous start-up package, modern research facilities, extensive shared equipment, and access to various state-of-the-art core facilities (https://rrc.uic.edu/cores/). Position Summary The Department of Biological Sciences at the University of\nIllinois Chicago invites\napplications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cell Biology. We seek\ncandidates who use any\ncombination of molecular, genetic, physiologic, and imaging approaches to\nexamine fundamental questions about cellular function across a wide range of\nmodel systems and biological scales. The successful candidate will be expected to establish a\nvigorous, externally funded research program. Commitment to teaching excellence\nin the graduate and undergraduate programs is expected. Teaching duties will\ninclude instruction at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with specific\ncourses to be determined. Duties & Responsibilities - Establish a vigorous, active, and externally funded research program utilizing any combination of experimental approaches to examine and explore processes fundamental to cellular biology in plant, animal, or microbial cells from any domain of life. - Participate in the intellectual life of the university. - Seek external funding in support of their research program. - Teach UIC undergraduate and graduate students in Biological Sciences. - Guide students in research. - Provide service to the Department and University in the form of committee work, seminar coordination, policy review, and/or mentorship and other service activities. - Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications The candidate must have a PhD degree, with relevant postdoctoral experience and\na demonstrated record of research accomplishments For\nfull consideration, please complete an online application and\nsubmit the following materials: - Cover letter outlining applicant qualifications and motivation - Curriculum vitae - Research plan (up to 3 pages) - Teaching philosophy statement (1 page) - Names and contact information (including email addresses) for at least 3 references Applications\nshould be submitted by December 18, 2026. Review of applications will\nbegin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Final\nauthorization of the position is subject to availability of funding. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20330?c=uic": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty- Greenhouse Management and Teaching",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty- Greenhouse Management and Teaching | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Clinical Faculty- Greenhouse Management and Teaching Chicago, IL, United States | 1041928 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/21/2026 - Application Deadline: 12/19/2026 Back to Search Clinical Faculty- Greenhouse Management and Teaching Hiring Department : Biological Sciences Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1041928 Posting Close Date : December 18. 2026 Salary: The\nbudgeted salary range for the position is $80,000 to $120,000. Salary is\ncompetitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also\nconsidering internal equity. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities, and\nit is ranked #1 in Illinois for social mobility. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. About the Plant Research Laboratory The UIC Plant Research Laboratory, operated by the\nDepartment of Biological Sciences, is a premier urban research facility\nsupporting biological research, education, and outreach. It features 3,600\nsquare feet of glasshouses on a one-acre outdoor area with experimental\ngardens. It also houses\nthe UIC Mobile Environmental Laboratory, which supports ecological research on\nurban vegetation, soils, microclimate, and atmospheric processes. Beyond\nits vital role in supporting UIC faculty and student research in plant ecology,\nevolution, and physiology, the facility supports undergraduate courses, and serves\nas a living laboratory that connects the campus community with the natural\nsciences. It also leads outreach activities beyond UIC through contributions to\nurban ecological monitoring, conservation projects, and school gardens\nthroughout the Chicago region. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary Assistant or Associate Rank Clinical Faculty position to serve as\nGreenhouse Manager for the Plant Research Laboratory (PRL). This is a\nrenewable, non-tenure track, full-time appointment that integrates operational\noversight of a shared research and teaching facility with undergraduate\ninstruction and student engagement. The position plays a central role in\nsupporting the teaching, research, and service missions of the department and\nuniversity. Position start date is flexible, preferably by May 2027. Duties & Responsibilities Greenhouse Operations - Oversee day-to-day greenhouse operations, including plant collections, environmental control systems, scheduling, safety, compliance, and coordination of users - Maintain greenhouse and selected outdoor spaces as functional environments for both research and teaching - Supervise staff and student workers in collaboration with departmental administration Teaching and Curriculum - Teach at least one course per semester based on the PRL grounds and greenhouses, focusing on botany, plant evolution, urban ecology, and/or related areas - Support laboratory modules and experiential components of existing BIOS courses - Maintain living collections and instructional materials in support of instruction on biodiversity and natural history Research and Student Support - Facilitate faculty- and student-led research projects using greenhouse resources - Advise on experimental setup, plant care, and basic methodological considerations - Support undergraduate research, independent study (BIOS 199/399) Outreach and Service - Manage and contribute to PRL’s role as a shared campus and community-facing resource that connects plant biology research and teaching with broader campus and external partnerships - Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications • Ph.D. in plant biology, ecology, evolutionary biology, or a closely\nrelated field • Demonstrated experience with greenhouse operations, plant care, or controlled-environment\nsystems • Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills Preferred Qualifications • Experience teaching at the undergraduate level • Demonstrated ability to integrate research facilities into curriculum and\nstudent projects • Practical knowledge of horticultural, mechanical, or environmental control\nsystems Application Instructions For\nfull consideration, please complete an on-line application, including a cover\nletter indicating qualifications relevant to greenhouse management, a\ncurriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy (and prior experience if\napplicable) focused on experiential instruction in plant biology, and the names\nand email addresses of three references. Posting will close\nDecember 18, 2026 at 5pm CST. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21106?c=uic": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor in Materials Chemistry",
      "description": "Associate or Full Professor in Materials Chemistry | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Associate or Full Professor in Materials Chemistry Chicago, IL, United States | 1043200 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 - Application Deadline: 12/15/2026 Back to Search Associate or Full Professor in Materials Chemistry Hiring Department : Chemistry Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043200 Salary:  The budgeted salary range for the position is $150,000 -\n$300,000.  This appointment is on a\nnine-month service basis with salary paid over twelve months. About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Job Summary The Department of Chemistry in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at the University of Illinois Chicago (UIC) invites applications for a tenured faculty position at the rank of associate or full professor, with a focus on experimental studies of materials under extreme conditions, including quantum materials. This strategic hire is intended to strengthen and expand materials research collaborations across UIC and with national laboratories, including Argonne National Laboratory (and the APS), Brookhaven National Laboratory (and NSLS-II), other U.S. Department of Energy laboratories, and partner universities through major interdisciplinary research centers and funded cooperative agreements. The anticipated start date is Fall 2027. Materials research faculty at UIC conduct both experimental and theoretical investigations spanning a broad range of topics, including quantum materials, energy materials, strongly correlated systems, advanced alloys, advanced manufactured materials, surfaces and low-dimensional systems, energetic materials, hard and superhard materials, nanomaterials, and biomaterials. UIC offers extensive computational, characterization, and synthesis capabilities through state-of-the-art core facilities, including advanced electron microscopies, materials synthesis laboratories, and high-performance computing resources. These strengths are complemented by access to world-class facilities at nearby national laboratories and partner institutions through longstanding collaborative relationships. The successful candidate will be expected to maintain a nationally and internationally recognized research program in materials chemistry, broadly defined. Relevant expertise may include, but is not limited to, materials at high pressure, low or high temperature, and high magnetic fields; quantum and other functional materials; the use of advanced radiation facilities, such as synchrotron, free-electron laser, large laser platforms, or neutron-scattering sources; and advanced microscopies.  The successful candidate will play a leadership role, or provide strong scientific leadership support, in advancing UIC's materials research enterprise and leveraging existing and emerging opportunities at national laboratories. The candidate will also have teaching duties consistent with their level of research activity, as per departmental and college policy. UIC is a Carnegie R1 public research university located in the heart of Chicago. Additional information about the Department of Chemistry and its research programs is available at chem.uic.edu. UIC is the largest university in the Chicago metropolitan area, serving more than 37,000 students across 15 colleges, including one of the nation's largest medical schools, and is recognized for having one of the most diverse student populations in the United States. Further information about the university and the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences can be found at uic.edu and las.uic.edu. Duties and Responsibilities • Create a vibrant research program in materials chemistry that contributes to and expands UIC's national and international recognized research in this area. • Conduct state-of-the-art experimental investigations of materials, with a focus on materials in extreme conditions broadly defined. • Provide strong scientific leadership support in advancing UIC's materials research enterprise and leveraging existing and emerging opportunities at national laboratories. • Perform other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications PhD in Chemistry or related discipline. It is anticipated that candidates currently hold tenure at the Associate Professor or Full Professor level, or possess equivalent senior research experience in a national laboratory or industrial research setting and have credentials suitable for a tenured appointment at the rank of full professor. Preferred Qualifications Relevant expertise may include, but is not limited to, materials at high pressure, low or high temperature, and high magnetic fields; quantum and other functional materials; the use of advanced radiation facilities, such as synchrotron, free-electron laser, large laser platforms, or neutron-scattering sources; and advanced microscopies. Application Instructions Applications must be submitted by December 15, 2026 .  Required application materials include: • Curriculum vitae • List of publications • Concise statement of research interests and future plans • Statement of teaching interests and philosophy • Names and contact information for at least three professional references. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20066?c=uic": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor-Pediatric Rheumatology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor-Pediatric Rheumatology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant/Associate/Professor-Pediatric Rheumatology Peoria, IL, United States | 1041638 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/24/2027 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Professor-Pediatric Rheumatology (Search extended through 1/24/2027) Hiring Department : UICOMP-Pediatrics Location :  Peoria, IL USA Requisition ID : 1041638 Posting Close Date : 9/6/2026 Salary: $175,500 to $216,233 per year The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria (UICOMP) seeks candidates for\nthe position(s) of Assistant/Associate/Professor-Pediatric Rheumatology  in the Department of Pediatrics. About\nthe University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria The\nUniversity of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is a regional campus of one\nof the largest public medical schools in the United States. We are known for\nhaving small class sizes and exceptional faculty mentorship. This allows UICOMP\nstudents to excel under a rigorous curriculum. In collaboration with our\nhospitals and clinical partners, UICOMP Faculty members provide care to more\nthan 45,000 patients each year. In addition, they contribute to medical\neducation and training for more than 260 students, and more than 300 physician\nresidents and fellows annually. UICOMP healthcare partners include Jump\nSimulation, a world-class leader in healthcare simulation and innovation, along\nwith OSF Saint Medical Center, OSF Children’s Hospital of Illinois and Carle\nHearth Greater Peoria. UICOMP is also part of a R1 research institute with\ntranslational research focusing on Alzheimer dementia and oncology. Learn\nmore about how the University of Illinois College of Medicine Peoria is helping\nto transform healthcare here: https://peoria.medicine.uic.edu/. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary Pediatric Rheumatologist to provide ambulatory and inpatient care to pediatric patients with rheumatologic illnesses at the Children's Hospital of Illinois. Duties & Responsibilities Provide acute and ongoing consultative care to children that have rheumatologic illnesses in both the hospital and outpatient settings. Participate in education and training programs for medical students and residents and fellows in the Department of Pediatrics Participate in Collaborative research activities of the Division of Rheumatology and department Perform other duties of a university faculty member including committee assignments, curriculum development and student counseling. Minimum Qualifications MD/DO Eligible for Illinois licensure BC/BE Pediatrics and/or Pediatric Rheumatology Preferred Qualifications Strong interest in education and clinical research. To apply, please\nvisit this job listing on the UIC Job Board at, https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/20066?c=uic , scroll towards the bottom of the page and click, “Apply\nNow”. You may be\nredirected to log into, or to create a new account. For fullest\nconsideration please apply by 11/13/2026. The budgeted salary\nrange for the position is $175,500 to $216,233 per year. Salary is\ncompetitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also\nconsidering internal equity. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
