    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21220?c=uic": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty - Department of Medicine, Divsision of Pulmonary, Critical Care, Sleep and Allergy",
      "description": "Open Rank Faculty - Department of Medicine, Divsision of Pulmonary, Critical Care, Sleep and Allergy | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Open Rank Faculty - Department of Medicine, Divsision of Pulmonary, Critical Care, Sleep and Allergy Chicago, IL, United States | 1043493 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/29/2026 - Application Deadline: 11/30/2026 Back to Search Open Rank Faculty, Department of Medicine, Division of Pulmonary Hiring Department : Medicine, Pulmonary, Critical Care, Sleep and Allergy Location :  Chicago, IL Requisition ID : 1043493 Salary: The budgeted salary range for the position is $237,060 - $310,000 About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Position Summary This\nis a full-time Adult Allergy and Immunology faculty position. The rank and\npromotion track will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience. The\nincumbent will provide comprehensive allergy and immunology care, participate\nin clinical program development, and contribute to the academic missions of\npatient care, teaching, research, and service. Responsibilities include caring\nfor patients with asthma, allergic rhinitis, food allergy, drug allergy,\nurticaria, eczema, immunodeficiency disorders, and other allergic and\nimmunologic conditions. Faculty members are expected to participate in\ndepartmental initiatives, quality improvement activities, interdisciplinary\ncollaborations, and educational programs. Duties &\nResponsibilities In\nthis position, the incumbent will provide patient care on a full-time basis, no\nless than forty hours per week, serving patients at the University of Illinois\nHospital and Health Sciences System (UI Health) and a medically underserved and\ndiverse patient population. Clinical responsibilities will include outpatient\nadult allergy and immunology clinics, evaluation and management of patients\nwith allergic, immunologic, and related disorders, interpretation of allergy\ntesting, and administration of allergy and immunotherapy services as\nappropriate. Additional clinical and scholarly opportunities may be considered\nbased on the candidate’s training and interests. The incumbent will assist the\nDepartment in teaching, training, and advising medical students, residents, and\nfellows in the fields of Internal Medicine, Allergy and Immunology, and related\ndisciplines. The candidate is expected to engage in medical science and/or\nmedical education research, with mentorship, in areas related to Allergy and\nImmunology. The candidate will also assist with curriculum development and\nperform university duties and administrative services as assigned. These\nactivities are essential components of an academic medicine program and are\nintegral to medical student education and resident/fellow training. Perform\nother related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications This\nposition requires a medical degree (MD, DO, or foreign equivalent), successful\ncompletion of an ACGME-accredited Internal Medicine residency program, and\ncompletion of an Allergy and Immunology fellowship program in the United\nStates. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible in Allergy and\nImmunology. A valid Illinois medical license or eligibility for an Illinois\nmedical license is required. Individuals who do not meet these minimum\nqualifications will not be considered for this position. Preferred Qualifications Preference\nwill be given to candidates with demonstrated interest or experience in adult\nallergy and immunology clinical practice, medical education, clinical research,\nquality improvement, or program development. Expertise in areas such as severe\nasthma, immunodeficiency, biologic therapies, food allergy, drug allergy, or\nallergy/immunology-related clinical research is desirable. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
    },
    "https://uic.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/21152?c=uic": {
      "title": "Open Rank Tenure Track Faculty - SPH Environmental and Occupational Health Sciences",
      "description": "Open Rank Tenure Track Faculty - SPH Environmental and Occupational Health Sciences | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Open Rank Tenure Track Faculty - SPH Environmental and Occupational Health Sciences Chicago, IL, United States | 1043352 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/29/2026 - Application Deadline: 1/1/2027 Back to Search Open Rank Tenure Track Faculty - SPH Environmental and Occupational Health Sciences Hiring Department : Environmental and Occupational Health Sciences (EOHS) Location :  Chicago, IL USA Requisition ID : 1043352 Salary:  The budgeted salary range\nfor the position is $95,000 - $200,000 About the University of Illinois Chicago UIC is among the nation’s preeminent urban public research universities, a Carnegie RU/VH research institution, and the largest university in Chicago. UIC serves over 34,000 students, comprising one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation and is designated as a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPSI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI).  Through its 16 colleges, UIC produces nationally and internationally recognized multidisciplinary academic programs in concert with civic, corporate and community partners worldwide, including a full complement of health sciences colleges. By emphasizing cutting-edge and transformational research along with a commitment to the success of all students, UIC embodies the dynamic, vibrant and engaged urban university. Recent “Best Colleges” rankings published by U.S. News & World Report, found UIC climbed up in its rankings among top public schools in the nation and among all national universities. UIC has over 300,000 alumni, and is one of the largest employers in the city of Chicago. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois Chicago is a vibrant and leading\npublic R1 institution in the heart of Chicago. The Division of Environmental\nand Occupational Health seeks applications for a faculty position to begin Fall\n2027: Open Rank Tenure Track\nFaculty (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) - Two positions Description: The University of Illinois Chicago (UIC)\nSchool of Public Health (SPH) Division of Environmental and Occupational Health\nSciences (EOHS) announces a search for two tenure-track faculty members at a\nrank commensurate with experience. The Division of Environmental and\nOccupational Health Sciences is one of four Divisions within the UIC SPH, the\nonly accredited school of public health in the state of Illinois. It is a\nleading research department within the school. Applicants at all levels should demonstrate\nresearch achievements in environmental and / or occupational health and the\nability to advance the Division’s teaching mission. The ideal candidates will\nhave experience obtaining research grant funding as a PI/Co-PI, success in\nteaching and mentoring graduate students, and a record of successful collaborations.  A strong scientific background in\nenvironmental and occupational health sciences or a related discipline is\nrequired. We are particularly interested in research and teaching experience in\nthe areas of exposure science, industrial hygiene, occupational safety,\nfarmworker health, the impacts of extreme weather on health, as well as air and\nwater quality. Other desirable assets include strong communications, team\nbuilding; experience teaching graduate students online, and evidence of\nsuccessful mentorship. This position is a 9-month salaried\nappointment with opportunities for summer research support.  The budgeted salary range for the\nposition is $95,000 - $200,000. The pay offered to the selected candidate will\nbe determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience\nand qualifications of the selected candidate including equivalent years in\nrank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market\npay for comparable jobs. Candidates must have: * A doctoral degree (or equivalent) in engineering, environmental science, epidemiology, industrial hygiene, occupational health, public health or a closely related field. * Peer-reviewed research publications and evidence of capacity to secure funding in the fields of occupational and /or environmental health sciences, appropriate for years of experience and job expectations. * Experience teaching and mentoring graduate students. * Interest in collaborative and multidisciplinary research. The EOHS division has a dynamic, multi-disciplinary and\nimpactful portfolio of research and service that reflect our values of\ncommunity engagement and the promotion of environmental and occupational\nhealth. Many\nopportunities exist at UIC for research collaboration with faculty in the\nfields of occupational safety, epidemiology, occupational medicine, community\nhealth, environmental health, and health policy. The EOHS division\nserves about 80 students in MPH, MS and PhD programs, with eight tenure-system\nfaculty, and twice that number of research and clinical faculty. Within the\nEOHS division, the NIOSH-funded Illinois Education and Research Center (ERC)\nsupports training, research, outreach and continuing education in a variety of\noccupational health disciplines; the NIOSH-funded Center for Healthy Work,\nwhich is using innovative engaged research methods to examine precarious work\nand its  impacts on health; and the Great\nLakes Center for Farmworker Health and Wellbeing which conducts research to\nimprove working conditions, fair and equitable wages, social protections, and\naccess to healthcare for farmworkers. The NIH-funded Center for Extreme\nConditions and Health Excellence supports interdisciplinary research and\ncommunity engagement addressing extreme weather and health including flooding\nand nature-based solutions. Other active areas of research include water\nquality and ambient air quality. UIC is one of the most diverse research-intensive\nuniversities in the United States, and is designated as a Minority Serving\nInstitution, an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving\nInstitute, and a Hispanic Serving Institution. The EOHS division is committed\nto ensuring access to graduate education for students who are diverse across\nmultiple dimensions, including: race, ethnicity, gender, age, disability,\ndisadvantages socioeconomic status, ideas and perspectives. We seek applicants\nthat will enrich and contribute to the diversity of the EOHS division and help\nus expand the perspectives and experiences we bring to our work. Application Process: Applicants must submit an on-line application using the link provided below.\nPlease upload a cover letter describing relevant experience and goals,\nteaching statement, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three\nreferences. For fullest consideration, all requested information must be\nsubmitted by January 1, 2027. Questions: Email Samuel Dorevitch, MD, MPH, Search Committee Chair\nat sdorevit@uic.edu. Only online applications will\nbe considered. Apply at [insert link here] by January 1, 2027. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. The university provides accommodations to applicants and employees. Request an Accommodation Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, covid sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. Select one: I am a current employee at UIC I am not a current employee at UIC I am a former employee at UIC Close Continue"
